.SH DEFAULT KEYBINDINGS
Keybindings can be customized in Fcitx5 Configuration → Addons → Vinput:
.TP
\f[B]Alt_R\f[R] (Trigger Key)
Tap to toggle recording start/stop; hold to push\-to\-talk (release to
finish).
.TP
\f[B]Control_R\f[R] (Command Key)
Hold after selecting text in any application to modify or rewrite the
selection using voice instructions.
.TP
\f[B]Shift_R\f[R] (Command Palette Key)
Open the unified interactive command palette with scoped slash filtering
(\f[CR]/a\f[R] for ASR, \f[CR]/s\f[R] for scenes, \f[CR]/m\f[R] for
command models, \f[CR]/p\f[R] for adapter processes) and global search.
.TP
\f[B]Page Up\f[R] / \f[B]Page Down\f[R], \f[B]Up\f[R] / \f[B]Down\f[R], \f[B]1\f[R]\-\f[B]9\f[R]
Navigate and select candidate text.
.SH RECOGNITION PIPELINE
.IP "1." 3
\f[B]Audio Capture\f[R]: Audio is captured from the selected PipeWire
input node.
.IP "2." 3
\f[B]VAD Trimming\f[R]: Leading and trailing silence is removed to
minimize latency.
.IP "3." 3
\f[B]ASR Inference\f[R]: Audio is transcribed by local sherpa\-onnx
models (offline) or external provider scripts (cloud).
.IP "4." 3
\f[B]Scene & LLM Post\-Processing\f[R]: If a non\-raw scene is active,
recognized text is formatted, corrected, or translated via an LLM.
.IP "5." 3
\f[B]Text Insertion\f[R]: Candidates are presented in the Fcitx5
candidate window and committed into the active application.
